diff --git a/voltana-llm-scripts/predictions/README.md b/voltana-llm-scripts/predictions/README.md
index 68921597..c465f6bd 100644
--- a/voltana-llm-scripts/predictions/README.md
+++ b/voltana-llm-scripts/predictions/README.md
@@ -21,3 +21,46 @@ Scripts are for A100 80G GPU. You may need to adjust `--mem-fraction-static` (in
 You can select the model to profile by modifying `p_server.sh`/`d_server.sh`/`run_profile.py`.
 
 After profiling, open and run `draw.ipynb` for result visualization and prediction model regression.
+
+## Run on a Slurm Cluster (L40S / L4)
+
+`slurm/profile.sbatch` starts the server and runs the profile inside one job on one GPU. It
+locks clocks with `sudo -n nvidia-smi -lgc` (passwordless sudo required, checked up front),
+maps the job's CUDA device to its NVML index for frequency locking/energy readings, resets
+clocks on exit, and logs actual SM clock / power / throttle reasons to `clocks-<jobid>.csv`.
+
+```shell
+conda activate voltanallm
+cd voltana-llm-scripts/predictions
+
+# prefill, all frequencies in one job (~1 h)
+sbatch --partition=<part> --gres=gpu:<l40s-type>:1 slurm/profile.sbatch prefill L40S
+
+# decode, one frequency per array task (default picks 5 supported clocks in [0.7 * max, max])
+sbatch --partition=<part> --gres=gpu:<l4-type>:1 --array=0-4 --time=08:00:00 slurm/profile.sbatch decode L4
+
+# or pin the frequencies explicitly (same list for every array task)
+FREQ_LIST=2040,1890,1740,1575,1425 sbatch ... slurm/profile.sbatch decode L4
+```
+
+Results go to `<prefill|decode>/results/<GPU_TAG>/<model>/<freq>/`; set `DATA_DIR` in the
+first loading cell of `draw.ipynb` to that directory. Fit L40S and L4 separately — the
+coefficients are hardware-specific. Before fitting, check `clocks-*.csv`: if the SM clock
+sits below the locked value (power cap, common on the 72 W L4), that frequency's data is
+not what its label says.
+
+Env overrides: `MODEL_PATH`, `FREQ_LIST`, `N_FREQ`, `FREQ_MIN_RATIO`, `MEM_FRACTION`,
+`CONTEXT_LEN`, `MAX_RUNNING`, `CUDA_GRAPH_MAX_BS`, `MAX_TOKENS`, `OUT_DIR`, `PORT`.
+Compute nodes usually have no internet: pre-download the model into a shared `HF_HOME`.
+
+The default model is `mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.1` (override with `MODEL_PATH`, a local path works too).
+It is gated on Hugging Face, so accept its terms and log in before downloading:
+
+```shell
+huggingface-cli download mistralai/Mistral-7B-v0.1
+```
+
+Notes for Mistral-7B-v0.1: it is a base model, so the benchmark warns about the missing chat
+template; this is harmless because requests use `ignore_eos` and fixed output lengths. SGLang
+serves it through the Llama implementation with full attention (its 4096-token sliding window is
+not applied), which is also how it will run when served, so the profiled latency stays consistent.
